## Course overview

Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches (AA) suits students who enjoy the elegance and rigour of mathematics and want strong algebraic and analytical skills. It emphasises proof, abstraction, and the power of calculus - ideal preparation for mathematics, engineering, the physical sciences, and economics at university.

## What you will study

- **Number and algebra**: sequences, proof, and complex numbers (HL).
- **Functions**: modelling and transformations.
- **Geometry and trigonometry**.
- **Statistics and probability**.
- **Calculus**: differentiation and integration, extended significantly at HL.

## Assessment

| Component | HL | SL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (no calculator) | 30% | 40% | Short and extended questions |
| Paper 2 (calculator) | 30% | 40% | Short and extended questions |
| Paper 3 (HL) | 20% | - | Extended problem-solving |
| Internal Assessment | 20% | 20% | A mathematical exploration on a topic of choice |

> Choose **AA** if you like proof and pure mathematics; choose **AI** if you prefer mathematics applied to real-world data and modelling.
